  the Gemma license terms with them.


3. DATASETS & BENCHMARKS — PULLED BY THE USER AT RUNTIME (NOT REDISTRIBUTED HERE)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No training datasets and (with one exception, noted below) no benchmark data are
redistributed in this repository. They are fetched by the user at runtime (e.g.
via `setup/prepare_data.sh` and `eval/prepare_benchmarks.py`):

Training datasets:
* mmr1 ........... no license declared on HuggingFace (null). Fetched at runtime.
* open_r1 ........ no license declared on HuggingFace (null). Fetched at runtime.
  Because no license is declared upstream, use is at the user's discretion under
  the source's terms; nothing from these datasets is redistributed here.

Evaluation benchmarks (fetched at runtime by eval/prepare_benchmarks.py):
* MathVision  (HF MathLLMs/MathVision)
* MathVerse   (HF AI4Math/MathVerse, testmini)
* We-Math     (HF We-Math/We-Math)
* MathVista   — Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike (CC BY-SA).
  A single-file subset (data/mathvista/testmini.jsonl, plus a 150-item in-loop
  selection subset) is the ONLY benchmark data bundled in this repo, included for
  offline checkpoint selection. Under CC BY-SA, attribution to the MathVista
  authors is required and any redistribution of this subset (which is internal
  only here) must remain under the same ShareAlike terms.


